{
  "id": "COMPOUND:15113 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking the compound [(3S,8S,10R,12R,13S,14R,17S)-17-acetyl-3,8,14,17-tetrahydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-1,2,3,4,7,9,11,12,15,16-decahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-12-yl] (E)-3-phenylprop-2-enoate] to the cell line SCCH-26 through a series of enzymatic targets. The compound is identified as a target of multiple enzymes, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is itself a target of Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and Basiliskamide B. These enzymes are involved in sialylation pathways, which are critical for cell surface glycoprotein function and signaling. The presence of multiple targets suggests a complex, possibly redundant, pathway that could contribute to the observed effect on SCCH-26. The evidence is supported by a consistent chain of targets, but the exact mechanism by which these enzymes influence SCCH-26 remains to be fully elucidated. The compound's role in this pathway is supported by its ability to interact with these enzymes, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm its direct effect on the cell line.",
